{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS53jW5pT7VADvahNWJH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll write ANSWER.md with the causes, what I changed, which parts of the colleague's note applied, and what you need to verify on your Mac."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":509,"cache_read_input_tokens":38837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":509},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9d5fac8-4014-497f-ac4e-f394fd4582df","uuid":"fca39d34-c2cc-434b-8ea7-8bb2f8f9a95a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:57:50.581Z","request_id":"req_011CgS53jFhh2onwHH6LjgXo"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS53jW5pT7VADvahNWJH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MNZMTHiGeT9B8jWwKsdBqt","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/h-Wap6zn/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why nightly-review never reported anything\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nThe job was running. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`,\nwhich matches the six failures in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`. The problem was\nnever that launchd didn't fire.\n\nTwo bugs stacked:\n\n1. **The agent could not run: `Not logged in · Please run /login`.** `claude -p`\n   failed on every run (exit 1). The plist's `EnvironmentVariables` sets only `PATH`,\n   with no `USER`. Under launchd the CLI could not find its login, which is the case the\n   colleague note describes. The snapshot shows the error but not the root cause, so\n   treat `USER` as the likely fix and confirm it with the verification steps below.\n2. **The failure reporter never ran: `read-only variable: status`.** The script\n   assigned `status=$?`. In zsh, `status` is a read-only alias of `$?`, so the\n   assignment at line 19 kills the script. It sits between the agent call and the\n   Telegram failure notice, so the failure is swallowed silently. I reproduced this in a\n   scratch HOME with the original script: the error appears and no notification is\n   sent.\n\nTogether these produce perfect silence: the job fails, and the only thing that could\nreport the failure is killed before it speaks.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`\n  - `status` renamed to `rc`, and the failure check now sits directly after the agent call.\n  - Agent stderr goes to a per-day `.err` file. The failure message includes its tail, so\n    the reason reaches your phone.\n  - An exit 0 with an empty report counts as a failure.\n  - Each run appends `rc`, duration in seconds, and output bytes to\n    `Library/Logs/nightly-review-runs.log`.\n  - `< /dev/null` on the `claude` call (defensive; see below).\n  - If the notifier itself fails, the script exits non-zero instead of pretending success.\n- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`: added `USER` = `vk` under\n  `EnvironmentVariables`. The plist paths use `/Users/vk`, so `vk` is my best guess for\n  the account name. Confirm it with `id -un` on the Mac.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\n- **Applied:** `status` is read-only in zsh and kills the script, which silenced the\n  failure notice. This was the main bug.\n- **Applied:** check `launchctl print` first. It showed runs and exit code, and the\n  `.err` log showed the real error.\n- **Applied:** `USER` missing from the plist → \"Not logged in\" → set `USER`.\n- **Applied:** log each run's duration, and treat empty output as failure, so a green\n  exit code with nothing done is caught.\n- **Applied:** put the failure notification directly after the failure path.\n- **Did not apply:** the stdin/prompt bug (\"Input must be provided…\"). The logs don't show\n  it, and the prompt is passed as an argument. The original script never got that far.\n  I kept the prompt as an argument and added `< /dev/null` only as defensive hardening.\n- **Not verified:** the external article and the claim that launchd does not pass\n  `USER`. I did not fetch them.\n\n## What I could not verify here\n\nI cannot run launchd or call your real `claude` and Telegram from this snapshot. Both\nfixes are verified only by a local simulation: a scratch HOME with fake `claude` and\n`notify.sh` (failure, success, empty-output, and notifier-failure cases all behave as\nintended), plus `plutil -lint` and `zsh -n`. The real test is on your Mac.\n\n## Steps on your Mac\n\n```sh\n# copy the fixed files from the snapshot into place\ncp bin/nightly-review.zsh ~/bin/nightly-review.zsh\ncp Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/\n\n# reload the plist so launchd picks up the new environment\nlaunchctl bootout gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist\nlaunchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist\n\n# run it now\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review\n```\n\nThen check all three:\n\n1. `launchctl print gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review` → `last exit code = 0`.\n2. `tail ~/Library/Logs/nightly-review-runs.log` → a new line with `rc=0`, a plausible\n   `seconds` (not 0–3), and `bytes` > 0. The report file\n   `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review-<today>.md` exists and is fresh.\n3. You received the \"done\" message on Telegram.\n\nIf it still says \"Not logged in\", `USER` was not the only cause. Check that `claude`\ncan log in non-interactively from launchd; `claude setup-token` may help, but keep any\ntoken in the keychain, not in the plist.\n\nTo test the failure path, temporarily make the job fail (for example, point `REPO` at a\nmissing directory with a bogus value), kickstart it, and confirm the \"FAILED\" message\narrives on Telegram. Then restore the file.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":509,"cache_read_input_tokens":38837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":509},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9d5fac8-4014-497f-ac4e-f394fd4582df","uuid":"673991e1-bbbd-425b-b0f1-1b1ce0f2c99b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:57:58.451Z","request_id":"req_011CgS53jFhh2onwHH6LjgXo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MNZMTHiGeT9B8jWwKsdBqt":{"file_path":"/tmp/h-Wap6zn/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why nightly-review never reported anything\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nThe job was running. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`,\nwhich matches the six failures in `Li