{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS54UoZqSvYbvhViAAoQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job ran every night and failed both times, but the failure report never got sent. Two bugs caused it.\n\n1. **The agent was not logged in.** `claude -p` exited 1 on all six runs with `Not logged in · Please run /login`. The launchd plist sets only `PATH`, with no `USER`. I added `USER` = `vk` to the plist. I guessed `vk` from the `/Users/vk` paths, so check it against `id -un` on your Mac.\n2. **The failure reporter was killed before it could run.** The script did `status=$?`. In zsh, `status` is read-only, so that line aborted the script at line 19, before the Telegram failure notice. I reproduced this locally with the original script: the error appears and no notification is sent.\n\n**Changes**\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: renamed the variable to `rc` and moved the failure check directly after the agent call. Agent stderr goes to a per-day `.err` file, and its tail is included in the failure message. An exit 0 with an empty report counts as a failure. Each run appends `rc`, duration, and output size to `nightly-review-runs.log`. If the notifier fails, the script exits non-zero.\n- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`: added `USER`.\n\n**Verification:** I can't run launchd or your real `claude` and Telegram from this snapshot. In a scratch HOME with fake `claude` and `notify.sh`, the failure, success, empty-output, and notifier-failure cases all behave as intended. `plutil -lint` and `zsh -n` pass. The real test is on your Mac.\n\n**From the colleague's note**\n- Applied: the `status` bug, checking `launchctl print` and the `.err` log first, the missing `USER`, duration logging, empty output as failure, and placing the failure notice right after the failure.\n- Not applied: the stdin \"Input must be provided\" bug. The logs don't show it. I added `< /dev/null` only as defensive hardeni